158169 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158263 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158263 #edb/ref 1061 32129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158263 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "458f5225-bfe2-5847-9c9c-043b6bc8cd45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158263 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186158543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158264 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158264 #edb/ref 1061 32131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158264 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b192d500-e629-54c1-bc67-397bce154d97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158264 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158265 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158265 #edb/ref 1061 32132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158265 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1d3f6450-2627-57f9-9c88-1e1c6ddb17b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158265 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158266 #edb/ref 1061 32133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158266 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e9bc56b9-0314-5f98-b64e-8cfbc787d859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158266 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158543 #edb/ref 1064 "Given the graph of a curve $y= f(x),$ there are two types of reflections we can apply to it:\n\n1\\. Reflection across the $y$-axis. This is a transformation of the form \n\n  $$\n  y=f(-x).\n  $$\n\n2\\. Reflection across the $x$-axis. This is a transformation of the form \n\n  $$\n  y=-f(x).\n  $$\n\nFor example, let's consider the function $y=f(x)$ below. \n\n![](images/69/6931216dd63985631394e3f3f2fe59246ddd810ecce5af0f0c7ad18b8634133b.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(-x)$ is a reflection of $y=f(x)$ in the $y$-axis, and it looks as follows:\n\n![](images/e2/e2274a68c25ed14ba93410fe87d672f85b839b7214b30e80d34a3ae28f47ef03.png)\n\n \n\nThe graph of $y=-f(x)$ is a reflection of $y=f(x)$ in the $x$-axis, and it looks as follows:\n\n![](images/ee/eee560bdd17899d55cdaea35204e9963ae9f0148f0ef897173e6250a3eb874b3.png)\n\n  \n\nWe can also combine reflections with other graph transformations. Let's see how." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158543 #edb/ref 1065 5125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158543 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f4bb9366-7e90-51e5-944c-9609c7607cfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158543 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
